<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Finding the probability for joint events</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p></p><p>The members of a wine tasting club are married couples. For any married couple in the club, the probability that the husband is retired is {@ret_hubby@} and the probability that the wife is retired {@ret_wife@}. Given that the wife is retired, the probability that the husband is retired is {@hubby_not_ret@}. For a randomly chosen married couple who are members of the club,</p><p>Find the probability that;</p><p>a) both of them are retired[[input:ans1]] (in 2 decimal places) [[validation:ans1]][[feedback:prt1]]</p><p>b) only one of them is retired[[input:ans2]]&nbsp;(in 2 decimal places) [[validation:ans2]][[feedback:prt2]]</p><p>c) neither of them is retired[[input:ans3]]&nbsp;(in 2 decimal places) [[validation:ans3]][[feedback:prt3]]</p><p>d) Two married couples are chosen at random, find the probability that only one of</p><p>the two husbands and only one of the two wives is retired[[input:ans4]] (in 2 decimal places) [[validation:ans4]][[feedback:prt4]]</p><p><br></p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Worked out solution <br></p><p>a) P(both of them are retired) = P(Husband retired &amp; Wife retired)&nbsp; = {@ret_hubby@}\(\times{@ret_wife@} = {@ta1@}\)<br></p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <br></p><p>b) P(only one of them is retired)=P(Husband retired &amp; Wife not retired) or P(Husband not retired &amp; Wife retired)=&nbsp;{@ret_hubby@}\(\times{@not_ret_wife@} +&nbsp;{@not_ret_hubby@}\times{@ret_wife@} = {@ta2@}\)<br></p><p><br></p><p>c) P(neither of them is retired)=P(wife not retired &amp; Husband not retired)=&nbsp;{@not_ret_wife@}\(\times{@hubby_not_ret@} = {@ta3@}\)</p><p><br></p><p>d)P(only one of the two husbands and only one of the two wives is retired)=P(Husband retired &amp; wife retired) or P((Husband retired &amp; Wife retired) &amp; (Husband not retired &amp; wife not retired))*2=&nbsp;{@ret_hubby@}\(\times{@ret_wife@}+&nbsp;{@ret_hubby@}\times{@ret_wife@}\times&nbsp;{@not_ret_hubby@}\times{@not_ret_wife@}\times{@2@} = {@ta4@}\)</p><p><br></p><p></p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
